From 6155a25b4663f81eb4e64b722dfd7a772a01bbd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:06:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/47] Z 6III: a release writes a JPEG to the card -- the
 still's capture models on by default

With the shutter type (custom setting d6) at "electronic shutter", a
release now goes all the way: capture, development, JPEG encode and the
camera's own record path, which writes DCIM/xxxNZ6_3/DSC_nnnn.JPG to the
CFexpress card -- 6048x4032 baseline JPEG, Exif "NIKON Z6_3", "Ver.02.00",
the picture the run's Bayer input holds (z9-capture-raw) -- and live view
resumes, showing that input. Release after release (three in a row tested,
plus two more with the defaults below). Under that shutter type the front
end raises image-available (sub_40F7102C) for the still, the capture
service's DC08 combinations start development (sub_4102D98C), and the
capture job (0x422D0001) ends as of a9df88f. At "auto", "mechanical" and
"electronic front-curtain" the image still takes the path a9df88f
describes, which waits for image outputs and does not complete here.

Three of ../z9-qemu's capture-model rules, written for one Z 9 capture
under instruction counting, refused this image's stills depending on
timing or on the release count (each a declined write; the last two stop
the machine). Under z63-still-capture:
  - the still's units are submitted (0x150c0060) before or after the
    bounded reset, depending on task timing, and committed after it with
    no new submission. The model kept only units 2 and 4 across a reset
    and refused the commit (0x150c0064 = 0x401e) otherwise; every
    submitted unit now keeps its parameters;
  - the still's 0x1543 output instance (0x15432000) ends each capture
    held (0x102) and is never stopped; the next still's mode 3 (0x103)
    found it active. Held, it has stopped at its frame boundary, and mode
    3 re-arms it;
  - this image encodes alternate stills on the second JPEG core
    (0x15e21000, JPEG_1, INTID 122, now wired); the model ran its one job
    on core 0. The job state stays single -- overlapping jobs are still
    refused -- and belongs to the core whose start (+4 = 1) claimed it,
    with that core's registers and line (also in nikon-z9-capture-nv16.h,
    now an edited header).
DECLARED, as the attachment's z63-still-capture block lists.

The board's default capture props (nikon-z63-z9lab.h) now add the
capture profile's models of ../z9-qemu and z63-still-capture, so
-machine z9-capture=on takes stills without a props list.

